---
// src/pages/about.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { YOUTUBE_URL } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The 206 Fix"
  description="What The 206 Fix is: a Seattle sports paper and retro gaming channel, built for the long view and the games we grew up on."
  activeNav=""
>
  <section class="border-b-4 border-double border-ink py-10">
    <div class="container-fix">
      <div class="kicker mb-2">The Masthead</div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[23px] leading-[1.25] tracking-[0.01em] text-ink max-md:text-[17px]">
        About The 206 Fix
      </h1>
      <p class="font-caslon text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-slate mt-4 max-w-[680px]">
        A Seattle sports paper with a pixel heart. A companion to the games we play and the games we grew up on.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="container-fix max-w-[760px]">
      <div class="prose-about font-body text-[10px] leading-[1.8]">
        <p class="dropcap">
          The 206 Fix started as two things that turned out to be one thing. A YouTube channel running no-commentary retro (NES/SNES) sports games. And to scratch the itch I had to write, something I love to do, about Seattle sports, something I love to watch.
        </p>

        <p>
          This site is the newspaper. The channel is the broadcast. They point at each other on purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>What you'll find here</h2>

        <p>
          Three layers, stacked like a real front page. There's the wire: aggregated Seattle sports news pulled from the best local writers and rumor desks, refreshed through the day so the front page is never stale. There's the desk: original columns, written slowly and deliberately, by me as I learn, on the Seahawks, Mariners, Kraken, and the Sonics. And there's the arcade: retro gaming coverage that ties back to the channel.
        </p>

        <h2>Why no commentary</h2>

        <p>
          Honestly? I'm new to this and this whole thing is a hobby/outlet for me. I have no desire to be YouTube famous or get my name out there. This is just something that is fun to me and let's me flex some writing muscles as a hobby while playing the video games I've always loved. It's my own little pixel world I get to share with you while we commiserate as Seattle fans in general. 
        </p>

        <h2>Why Seattle</h2>

        <p>
          Because that's my home town. And I miss it a lot. I grew up there and was inextricably amalgamated into what I consider to be the greatest sports culture from the Big 4 sports; Baseball, Football, Basketball and Hockey. Sure, I'm biased. But I love my hometown and though I live away now, I hope to one day return to it. In the meantime, I get to play games and write about the teams and players I love for the city that will always be my home. 
        </p>

        <h2>Who writes this</h2>

        <p>
          For now, the byline is the area code. The writing matters more than the name attached to it, and the name can come later. What you need to know is at some point, as I spread my wings, assuming this ever goes anywhere, I will bring you into the fold as we get to know each other. Just know that I bleed Seattle sports and the perspective I write from is one that is shared, for better or worse, by the entire 206 loving world. The greater sports media world never gives us our due, even after 1 basketball title (lost the team), 2 Super Bowls and counting, a broken playoff drought and a Kraken team that I believe has a great future, we still get relegated to the back page. Well, long live Seattle sports and screw those who give bad teams more press. 
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-ink flex flex-wrap gap-5 justify-between items-center">
        <a href="/" class="font-pixel text-rust text-[18px] hover:text-forest">&laquo; Front Page</a>
        <a href={YOUTUBE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-pixel text-[18px] bg-rust text-cream px-6 py-3 hover:bg-forest transition-colors">
          Watch on YouTube &#9654;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .prose-about p { margin-bottom: 1.3em; }
  .prose-about h2 {
    font-family: 'Press Start 2P', monospace;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-top: 1.8em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
    color: var(--forest);
  }
  .prose-about .dropcap::first-letter {
    font-family: 'Press Start 2P', monospace;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 34px;
    float: left;
    line-height: 0.85;
    padding: 6px 8px 0 0;
    color: var(--forest);
  }
</style>
